{
  "_audit": [
    "Audit: B.9.3 (b9-3-shared-oidc, FR-GL-B9-3-020/021, ADR-B9-3-002)",
    "",
    "ONE issuer, TWO client registrations. `issuer`, `scopes` and `discoveryUrl` are",
    "declared HERE, once. Each surface carries only what genuinely differs: its own",
    "clientId and redirectUri. A native custom-scheme redirect and a browser https",
    "redirect are normally two separate client entries at the provider — modelling",
    "them as one tuple would be wrong for the common case.",
    "",
    "NO SECRET BELONGS IN THIS FILE. Both surfaces are PUBLIC clients using PKCE",
    "(RFC 8252 for the app, RFC 6749 §2.1 for the browser). There is no client_secret",
    "to configure, and a secret committed here would be readable by anyone who",
    "installs the app or opens devtools (Article X.2).",
    "",
    "T3 GAP (FR-B9-3-040, ADR-B9-3-004). .forge/standards/identity.yaml is",
    "compliance_tier_aware and states that tier T3 requires a SELF-HOSTED identity",
    "provider. mobile-pwa-first is layer_profile client-only: it has no infra layer",
    "and can self-host nothing. If you are operating at T3, that obligation does not",
    "disappear — it transfers to the provider deployment you run separately from",
    "this repository. The standard is not edited to accommodate this archetype.",
    "",
    "SESSIONS ARE INDEPENDENT, NOT SSO. A token minted in the native app is not",
    "available to the PWA and vice versa: they are different clients holding",
    "different sessions. See web-pwa/README.md.",
    "",
    "`offline_access` APPLIES TO BOTH SURFACES, AND THAT IS A TRADE-OFF WORTH A",
    "DECISION. It is what makes the native app able to refresh silently, and it is",
    "correct there: the token lands in Keychain / encryptedSharedPreferences. The PWA",
    "receives one too, holds it in memory only, and loses it on reload. It buys the",
    "browser a longer session (past access-token expiry, until reload) at the cost of",
    "a long-lived credential sitting in the JS heap, where an XSS can read and replay",
    "it offline. If you would rather the PWA session simply end at access-token",
    "expiry, drop `offline_access` here and accept that the native surface loses",
    "silent refresh too — `scopes` is deliberately declared ONCE",
    "(FR-GL-B9-3-020), so today the two surfaces cannot diverge on it. Splitting",
    "scopes per surface is a schema change, not a setting."
  ],
  "issuer": "TODO_REPLACE_ISSUER_URL",
  "scopes": ["openid", "profile", "email", "offline_access"],
  "discoveryUrl": null,
  "surfaces": {
    "app": {
      "clientId": "TODO_REPLACE_APP_CLIENT_ID",
      "redirectUri": "<reverse-domain>://callback"
    },
    "web-pwa": {
      "clientId": "TODO_REPLACE_WEB_PWA_CLIENT_ID",
      "redirectUri": "https://TODO_REPLACE_WEB_PWA_ORIGIN/auth/callback"
    }
  }
}
